id: DRAFT-12776-kea-admin-3.0.3-ohos-ksh93-arith-cmdsubst-doubling
title: OHOS /system/bin/sh（Korn 系）算术展开内嵌命令替换翻倍命令名（$(( $(date +%s) + n )) → datedate）：等待/超时类 shell 逻辑立即误判超时
category: ohos, portability, shell, testing
build_system: shell|meson
phase: testing
match_keywords: /system/bin/sh, ksh93, mksh, tracked alias, arithmetic expansion, arithmetic command substitution, $(( )), $(date +%s), deadline, timeout, wait_for_file, wait_for_process_to_stop, datedate, bad uid, memfile, kea-dhcp4
error_signature: "datedate.*not found|echoecho.*not found|bad uid|.*was not created in time"
error_excerpt: "On the OHOS device, /system/bin/sh (Korn-family shell; its banner lists 'tracked aliases', e.g. 'date is an alias for date') mis-tokenizes a command substitution nested inside an arithmetic expansion: `local deadline=\"$(($(date +%s) + timeout))\"` executes `date` as `datedate` (sh -x trace: '+ datedate +%s', stderr 'datedate: inaccessible or not found'), the substitution yields empty and the arithmetic proceeds with the empty value, so deadline collapses to `4`. Any wait-helper then compares 4 against the current epoch and declares immediate timeout: upstream Kea memfile.init fails with 'kea-dhcp4.csv was not created in time' although the server starts fine. Minimal repro: `d=$(( $(echo 5) + 4 ))` -> 'echoecho: inaccessible or not found'; `$(( $(id -u) + 4 ))` -> 'id: bad uid 20020084'."
affected_scope: 一切在 OHOS 上执行、脚本内含形如 $(( $(cmd) + n )) 嵌套命令替换的 shell 测试套件/交付脚本（等待/超时/deadline 计算最常见；不限于 Kea；纯算术与算术外比较不受影响）。kea 3.0.3 全树 7 处 $(( 仅 2 处嵌套命中：修复前 memfile.init 确定性失败，补丁 0009 后 3/3 通过。
root_cause: "The OHOS /system/bin/sh (Korn-family, tracked-alias semantics) duplicates the command word when a `$(...)` command substitution appears inside `$((...))` arithmetic expansion. The command is emitted twice ('date' -> 'datedate'), the (failed) substitution evaluates as empty, and arithmetic continues as if the value were 0. The bug only fires for the nested form `$(( $(cmd) ... ))`; plain `test x -lt \"$(date +%s)\"` and hoisted `now=$(date +%s); $((now + n))` are unaffected. Pattern is common in upstream wait/timeout helpers."
rec_approach: "Hoist the command substitution OUT of the arithmetic expansion into a variable first: `now=$(date +%s)` then `deadline=$((now + timeout))`. When porting packages that run upstream shell suites (or ship shell scripts), grep for the nested pattern `\\$\\(\\s*\\$\\(` and rewrite every hit; do not rely on `env -i`, `unalias`, or bypassing PATH - the mis-tokenization happens before command lookup and cannot be aliased away."
solution: "kea-admin 3.0.3 patch 0009 (archives/k/kea-admin/3.0.3/patches/0009-*.patch) rewrites the two affected lines in src/lib/testutils/dhcp_test_lib.sh.in (wait_for_file, wait_for_process_to_stop). Full-tree scan showed only these 2 of 7 `$((` sites were nested; the other 5 (pure arithmetic) are safe. After the patch the upstream memfile suite runs 3/3 (memfile.version/init/upgrade OK, 12.71 s)."
fallback: "If rewriting the upstream helper is undesirable, wrapper forms work: `test 5 -lt \"$(date +%s)\"` (comparison outside arithmetic) and pre-hoisting both operands. Prefer the upstream patch so the same suite run is reproducible by reviewers."
prescan_pattern: "\\$\\(\\([^)]*\\$\\("
verify_builds: "kea-admin 3.0.3 (task 12776, 2026-10-04): probe arith_probe.sh on HarmonyOS PC (datedate/echoecho/bad uid reproduced; hoist fixed); after patch 0009, meson memfile_tests.sh 3/3 OK on device"
doc_file: knowledge/drafts/DRAFT-12776-kea-admin-3.0.3-ohos-ksh93-arith-cmdsubst-doubling.md
draft: true
severity: 2
last_updated: 2026-10-04
